  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=13604\n\nIn at least Firefox and Chrome, we have `form.hasOwnProperty(\"a\")` is true, but `\"a\"` does not show up in the own property keys. (I haven't tested Safari.)\n\nFrom what I can tell of https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#legacy-platform-object-ownpropertykeys, this should be impossible. (We worked on this in https://github.com/whatwg/webidl/issues/400.)\n\n`HTMLFormElement` is a special snowflake since it uses `LegacyOverrideBuiltIns` and `LegacyUnenumerableNamedProperties`. But this shouldn't let it break these rules.\n\nMy guess is that multiple browsers have a bug where they're interpreting `LegacyUnenumerableNamedProperties` as not only hiding from `Object.keys()` (which filters to enumerable), but also hiding from `Object.getOwnPropertyNames()`.\n\nI think the compat risks of fixing this should be low since `Object.getOwnPropertyNames()` is used quite rarely.",
